## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | docs/agents/bug_development_dynamic_repo.md | ⚠️ important sm wiring doc guides projects into a permanently locked idempotency label the wiring instruction says the dynamic rule should use its own skipiflabel addlabel idempotency pair but the variant inherits the parent s sm label cleanup unchanged bug development json 24 sets customparams removelabel sm bug development triggered and js developbugandcreatepr js 109 removelabels removes exactly that one label on every terminal — normal fix interrupted gh 742 reset for retry blocked already fixed pr already open — with the stated purpose to avoid permanent lock js developbugandcreatepr js 817 the factory invariant is that the dispatching rule s addlabel skipiflabel value equals the agent s customparams removelabel see sm json 112 118 for the default bug rule if a project follows this doc and picks a fresh label value the natural reading of its own pair the dynamic rule s dispatch label is never removed by any terminal skipiflabel keeps matching forever so the dynamic lane — the only lane enabled for the ticket since the doc also disables the default bug rule — never re arms it silent consequences interrupted leg resets the ticket to ready for development for automatic retry but the retry can never fire rework legs review changes → back to development never dispatch the gh 1301 ask exit deliberately keeps customparams removelabel as the rule s only skip guard — for this variant that guard is the wrong parent s label fixes any one a document that the rule s skipiflabel addlabel value must equal the inherited customparams removelabel sm bug development triggered or that the project must override removelabel variant config or agentparampatches to match its new label b override removelabel in bug development dynamic repo json and tell projects to use that value c drop the its own pair wording note the same sentence exists in the two story variant docs — worth fixing there too but this pr only owns the bug variant |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | docs/agents/generated/bug_development_dynamic_repo.md | 💡 suggestion prompt snapshot never committed — this generated doc is missing the prompt snapshot section its siblings have the generator emits snapshots bug development dynamic repo md verified node generate agent snapshots js produces it — all 75 snapshots this is the only one absent from the tree every other tracked agent has its snapshot committed including all three dynamic repo siblings snapshots story development dynamic repo md story test automation dynamic repo md story development dynamic repo test md pr 1533 added it for its agent because js agentdocgenerator js links the snapshot only when the file already exists the regenerated doc for this agent lacks the prompt snapshot section lm step bullet that e g docs agents generated bug development md 33 35 and story test automation dynamic repo md 39 41 carry ci stays green — the docs freshness check github workflows agent docs yml 47 uses git diff exit code which cannot see an untracked new file verified removing the snapshot and re running both generators exits 0 — so the staleness will silently persist on main until someone runs the generator and notices a dirty tree fix run node js agentdocgenerator js node generate agent snapshots js and commit snapshots bug development dynamic repo md the regenerated doc with its new snapshot section |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

